  "body": "Found while fixing #1604.\n\n**What happens:** the post stream states the stock only as its axis-aligned box (`StockXYLeft/Right/Front/Back`, `StockZTop`). The fix for #1604 in `assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps` uses the largest half-width of that box as the stock's radius about the spindle axis. That is exact for a round bar. A box stock (a square bar) turned on a lathe sweeps a circle of half its diagonal, so its rotating corners stand outside the radius the post uses. The departure before G30 (`+X` to the stock's diameter) and the approach after G30 can then pass inside the corners' circle.\n\n**Why the post cannot fix it alone:** the stream does not say if the stock is a round bar or a box. Half the diagonal for every stock puts every turning start \"inside\" a round bar (a start at Ø12.1 on a Ø12 bar is inside Ø16.97), so every turning program would be refused.\n\n**Expected:** the stream states the stock's turning radius about the work-offset Z axis (for example a `StockTurnRadius` PARAM from `post::dump`, the swept radius of the stock shape), and `tormach-lathe.cps` (and `fanuc-lathe.cps` where it applies) uses it in place of the box's half-width.\n\n**Workaround:** use a round-bar (cylinder) stock for lathe setups.\n\n**Done means:** a lathe stream states the stock's turning radius; the Tormach lathe post's G30 approach and departure use it; a pin with a square-bar stock shows no G30-adjacent rapid inside the corners' circle.\n\nRelated: #1604.\n",
